From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andriy Chuma <chuma.andriy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] m68k: flippies: Add the real-time clock and error light
 drivers

Add drivers for two devices of the Create Flippies PC that the platform
code registers:

- rtc-flippies: the real-time clock, a 64-bit count of seconds since the
  Unix epoch that keeps running while the PC is reset or switched off.
  Reading SECONDS_LO latches SECONDS_HI, and writing SET_HI sets the
  clock to SET_HI:SET_LO. It has no alarm and no interrupt.
- leds-flippies: the error light on the case, bit 0 of the system
  controller's LEDS register, as the LED class device flippies::fault.
  The case shows it together with the emulator's own error conditions,
  so software in the PC can light it to report a fault. It is a panic
  indicator too. It binds to the system controller device; reset and
  power off stay in the platform code.
---
